# .env.testing is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It exists because of a real M9 mistake: without it, --env=testing
# loaded .env, and `migrate:fresh --seed --env=testing` dropped the
# development database. The file must reach every developer and CI or the
# trap comes back for whoever clones next.
#
# It holds local test-database values that already appear in .env.example
# and match phpunit.xml, and DestructiveDatabaseGuardTest asserts the two
# stay in step. No production secret belongs in it.
!.env.testing
